step Heavy Armor Kit to 150
  tip Heavy Armor Kit is orange at 140 (yellow 145, green 155, grey 165): about 11 crafts to 150, up to 13 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 5 Heavy Leather and 1 Fine Thread. Five Heavy Leather a craft (beasts of level 28-40); the kits sell to vendors. Leatherworking 150 is a Legacy System milestone.
  craft 3780 until 150
  skill Leatherworking 150

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Expert (150-225)
section Leatherworking 150-225

step Leatherworking 150-225: vendor goods
  tip Buy the whole bracket's share in one go: 29 Fine Thread (29s), 15 Salt (7s 50c) and 145 Silken Thread (7g 25s); about 7g 61s 50c in all. The arrow picks the nearest seller of your faction (Stormwind City: Edna Mullby and Jillian Tanner; Orgrimmar: Felika, Shimra and Tamar).
  buy 2321 x29 nearest
  buy 4289 x15 nearest
  buy 4291 x145 nearest

step Expert Leatherworking
  tip Expert raises the cap from 150 to 225; it needs Leatherworking 125 and character level 20, so you can take it on any visit from 125. Only a few trainers teach it: Alliance Telonis (Darnassus); Horde Una (Thunder Bluff). This route trains it at Telonis (Darnassus) for the Alliance and Una (Thunder Bluff) for the Horde, who also teach the recipes of 150-225: one trainer for every visit. Learn now: Barbaric Shoulders (from 150). 150-225 takes about 7g 61s 50c of vendor goods, plus 398 Thick Leather to gather or buy. The gathering steps below come between the visits: learn each recipe when you are back for it. Nightscape Pants (from 205) takes a second trip, to other trainers (below).
  level 20
  train Leatherworking Expert npc 4212 only Alliance
  train Leatherworking Expert npc 3007 only Horde
  learn 7151 npc 4212 only Alliance
  learn 7151 npc 3007 only Horde

step Skinning 236-250: Beasts 35-45
  tip Skin from Skinning 236 to 250 for Heavy Armor Kit: this area gives Heavy Leather, and the next one the rest from Skinning 250. The window lists the areas for your level, best first: the arrow leads to the one you pick and rests once you are in it; each keeps to creatures no more than a level above you and away from the other faction's towns.
