step Rugged Armor Kit to 239
  tip Rugged Armor Kit is yellow at 225 (yellow 225, green 235, grey 245): about 23 crafts to 239, up to 29 for 9 players in 10 (the gathered materials above count that many). Each takes 5 Rugged Leather. Five Rugged Leather a craft. Specialisation (optional): at 225 and character level 40. Dragonscale: Peter Galen (Azshara) or Thorkaf Dragoneye (Badlands) wants 2 Tough Scorpid Breastplates, 2 Tough Scorpid Gloves (patterns drop from the Wastewander bandits in Tanaris) and 10 Worn Dragonscale. Elemental: Sarah Tanner (Searing Gorge) or Brumn Winterhoof (Arathi Highlands) wants 2 each of Heart of Fire, Globe of Water, Core of Earth and Breath of Wind. Tribal (also from 225, as Forever's quest data asks): Caryssia Moonhunter (Feralas) or Se'Jib (Stranglethorn Vale) wants a Wild Leather Vest and Helmet, after the Wild Leather quests from Pratt McGrubben or Jangdor Swiftstrider in Feralas. On Forever the specialisation patterns need a Tanning Rack. You can take only one; none is needed for 300, and the beta never tested them (it stopped at level 30).
  craft 19058 until 239

